$$************************************************************************************************** 
************************************** GENERAL INFORMATION *****************************************
****************************************************************************************************

Script Strain induced precipitates according to Tutorial 21.
The following contents will be covered:

 - Introduction of deformation into the thermo-mechanical treatment
 - Effect of volumetric misfit on precipitation kinetics
 - Effects of the applied deformation on the precipitation kinetics

Deformation process influences the microstructure of the alloy. One of the effects is the occurence 
of the strain induced precipitates. This tutorial demonstrates how the deformation processes can be 
included in the simulation of the processed material. Moreover, the effects of the deformation on the 
precipitation kinetics are demonstrated and discussed.

Database: mc_fe.tdb, mc_fe.ddb
Author: M. Lueckl
Creation date: 17.02.2017
Last update: 24.06.2019 (P. Warczok, Update for 6.02)
This is a script for MatCalc version 6.02 (rel 1.003)

Known issues:
- "save-workspace "file-name"=Tutorial_21" is not working properly. Use "save-workspace Tutorial_21" instead.


****************************************************************************************************
************************************** SETUP INFORMATION *******************************************
**************************************************************************************************$$

use-module module-name=core                                                                                                              $ Select core module for kinetic simulation
close-workspace options=f                                                                                                                $ Close any open workspace without asking for save 

new-workspace                                                                                                                            $ Create a new workspace 

$ Add some information about your Script
@echo value=no
set-workspace-info information=Script T20
set-workspace-info information=+Simulating grain growth
set-workspace-info information=+using the single-class model

echo value=y

$$************************************************************************************************** 
**************************************** SYSTEM SETUP **********************************************
**************************************************************************************************$$



$$************************************************************************************************** 
                          DATABASES, CHEMICAL COMPOSITION, SELECTED PHASES
**************************************************************************************************$$

open-thermodynamic-database file-name=mc_fe.tdb                                                                                          $ Thermodynamic database
select-elements elements=Fe C Nb                                                                                                         $ Elements
select-phases phases=bcc_a2 fcc_a1 cementite                                                                                             $ Phases
read-thermodynamic-database  

set-reference-element element=Fe
enter-composition type=weight-percent composition=c=0.2 nb=0.04

read-mobility-database file-name=mc_fe.ddb                                                                                               $ Mobility database

set-automatic-startvalues 
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1000                                                                                                 $ Temperature 1000C
calculate-equilibrium                                                                                                                    $ Initial equilibrium


$$**************************************************************************************************
                                 STEPPED EQUILIBRIUM CALCULATIONS
**************************************************************************************************$$

set-step-option type=temperature                                                                                                         $ Step equilibrium calculation type
set-step-option range start=1400 stop=400 scale=lin step-width=10                                                                        $ Define the temperature range and the step
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                                                               $ Temperature in celsius
step-equilibrium                                                                                                                         $ Performs stepped equilibrium calculation


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                       GRAPHICAL OUTPUT
**************************************************************************************************$$

new-gui-window type-id=p1                                                                                                                $ Create plot window
move-gui-window displace window-id=. x-origin=150 y-origin=100 width=600 height=500                                                      $ Move and resize plot window

$ define default x-axis properties
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-title=Temperature / °C                                                                $ Axis title
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-data=T$c                                                                              $ X-axis data

$ define plot properties: phase fraction
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Phase fraction                                                                                    $ Axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-type=log                                                                                                $ Type: log
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=f$*                                                                            $ Add series

update-gui-window window-id=.                                                                                                            $ Update the GUI window
set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                                                                       $ Duplicate and lock all series

$ Remove all duplicated series
set-plot-option plot-id=1 series remove series-index=-1 series-name=f$fcc_a1
set-plot-option plot-id=1 series remove series-index=-1 series-name=f$fcc_a1#01
set-plot-option plot-id=1 series remove series-index=-1 series-name=f$bcc_a2
set-plot-option plot-id=1 series remove series-index=-1 series-name=f$cementite


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                 PRECIPITATION DOMAIN AND PHASES
**************************************************************************************************$$

$ ---------------------------------- PRECIPITATION DOMAIN ------------------------------------------
create-precipitation-domain new-domain-name=austenite                                                                                    $ Creates precipitation domain "austenite"
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=austenite thermodynamic-matrix-phase=fcc_a1                                       $ Austenite domain structure: fcc

$ -------------------------------------- PRECIPITATE -----------------------------------------------
create-new-phase parent-phase=fcc_a1#01 precipitate                                                                                      $ Creates NbC precipitate
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 nucleation-sites=dislocations                                        $ Nucleation sites at dislocations


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                    THERMOMECHANICAL TREATMENT
**************************************************************************************************$$

create-tm-treatment tm-treatment-name=cooling                                                                                            $ Create the heat treatment sequence

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=cooling                                                                                             $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=cooling tm-treatment-segment=. segment-start-temperature=1300                                         $ Start temperature is set 1300C
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=cooling tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=750 temperature-gradient=-1        $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=cooling tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                         $ Precipitation domain


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                       GRAPHICAL OUTPUT
**************************************************************************************************$$

$-------------------------------------------- Setup GUI -------------------------------------------$
$-- (Following part is copied from /scripts/frame_scripts/03_kinetics_4_frames_T_f_n_r_linX.mcs ) -$

new-gui-window p1                                                                                                                        $ create plot window
move-gui-window displace . 75 15 880 790                                                                                                 $ move and resize plot window

$ define default x-axis properties
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-for-all-plots=yes
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-title="time / s"
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-type=lin

set-gui-window-property . number-of-plot-columns=auto

$ define plot properties: temperature profile
set-plot-option . y-axis-title="temperature / C"
set-plot-option . series new buffer T$C

$ define plot properties: phase fraction
create-new-plot xy-plot .
set-plot-option . use-alias-names-in-legend=yes            
set-plot-option . series new buffer f_prec$*
set-plot-option . y-axis-title="phase fraction"

$ define plot properties: number density
create-new-plot xy-plot .
set-plot-option . use-alias-names-in-legend=yes            
set-plot-option . series new buffer num_prec$*
set-plot-option . y-axis-title="number density / m<sup>-3</sup>"
set-plot-option . y-axis-type=log
set-plot-option . y-axis-scaling=1e10..

$ define plot properties: mean radius
create-new-plot xy-plot .
set-plot-option . use-alias-names-in-legend=yes
set-plot-option . series new buffer r_mean$*
set-plot-option . y-axis-title="mean radius / nm"
set-plot-option . y-axis-type=log
set-plot-option . y-axis-scaling=1e-1..
set-plot-option . y-axis-factor=1e9

$---------------------------------- (end of the copied file) --------------------------------------$

$ Modification of temperature plot
set-plot-option plot-id=2 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=2 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines

$ Modification of phase fraction plot
set-plot-option plot-id=3 y-axis-type=log                                                                                                $ Log scale
set-plot-option plot-id=3 y-axis-scaling=1e-10..0.001                                                                                    $ Rescale axis
set-plot-option plot-id=3 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=3 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines

$ Modification of number density plot
set-plot-option plot-id=4 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=4 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines

$ Modification of mean radius plot
set-plot-option plot-id=5 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=5 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                       KINETIC CALCULATION
**************************************************************************************************$$

set-simulation-parameter tm-treatment-name=cooling                                                                                       $ Define the max. temperature step
start-precipitate-simulation

set-gui-window-property window-id=3 duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                                                                       $ Duplicate an lock all series

set-plot-option plot-id=2 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=Cooling                                               $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=3 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC                                            $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=4 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC                                            $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=5 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC                                            $ Rename series 

rename-current-buffer new-buffer-name=cooling                                                                                            $ Give the buffer a new name


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                    EFFECT OF VOLUMETRIC MISFIT
**************************************************************************************************$$

create-calc-buffer new-buffer-name=Vol_misfit                                                                                            $ Create a new buffer
set-gui-window-property window-id=3 buffer-name=Vol_misfit                                                                               $ Assign the buffer to the plot 

$ -------------------------------------- PRECIPITATE -----------------------------------------------
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 volumetric-misfit=0,1                                                $ Use volumetric misfit between prec./matrix 
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 use-volumetric-misfit-in-nucleation=yes 	                            $ Take volumetric misfit into account during nucleation 

$ ----------------------------------- KINETIC CALCULATION ------------------------------------------
set-simulation-parameter tm-treatment-name=cooling                                                                                       $ Define the max. temperature step
start-precipitate-simulation
set-gui-window-property window-id=3 duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                                                                       $ Duplicate an lock all series

set-plot-option plot-id=2 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=Cooling                                               $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=3 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC(misfit)                                    $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=4 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC(misfit)                                    $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=5 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC(misfit)                                    $ Rename series 


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                 SIMULATION OF DEFORMATION PROCESS
**************************************************************************************************$$

create-calc-buffer new-buffer-name=Deformation                                                                                           $ Create a new buffer
set-gui-window-property window-id=3 buffer-name=Deformation                                                                              $ Assign the buffer to the plot 

$ ---------------------------------- PRECIPITATION DOMAIN ------------------------------------------
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=austenite subgrain-evolution-model=abc                                            $ Sherstnev-Kozeschnik simple

$ -------------------------------------- PRECIPITATE -----------------------------------------------
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 ignore-volumetric-misfit-during-deformation=yes                      $ Ignore volumetric misfit during deformation 

$ --------------------------------- THERMOMECHNICAL TREATMENT --------------------------------------
create-tm-treatment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                        $ Create the heat treatment sequence

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. segment-start-temperature=1300                                     $ Start temperature is set 1300C
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=1000 temperature-gradient=-1   $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
$ In the current segment [.], Accumulated strain of 0.7 is set
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. segment-accumulated-strain=0.7                                     $ Accumulated strain
$ In the current segment [.], deformation rate of 0.15 s-1 is set
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. deformation-rate=0.15                                              $ Strain rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=950 temperature-gradient=-1    $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
$ In the current segment [.], Accumulated strain of 0.7 is set
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. segment-accumulated-strain=0.7                                     $ Accumulated strain
$ In the current segment [.], deformation rate of 0.15 s-1 is set
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. deformation-rate=0.15                                              $ Strain rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=900 temperature-gradient=-1    $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
$ In the current segment [.], Accumulated strain of 0.7 is set
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. segment-accumulated-strain=0.7                                     $ Accumulated strain
$ In the current segment [.], deformation rate of 0.15 s-1 is set
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. deformation-rate=0.15                                              $ Strain rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                         $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=750 temperature-gradient=-1    $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=deformation tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                     $ Precipitation domain

$ ----------------------------------- KINETIC CALCULATION ------------------------------------------
set-simulation-parameter tm-treatment-name=deformation                                                                                   $ Define the max. temperature step
start-precipitate-simulation

set-plot-option plot-id=2 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=T$C new-name=Deformation                                             $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=3 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC(deform)                                    $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=4 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC(deform)                                    $ Rename series 
set-plot-option plot-id=5 series rename series-index=-1 series-name=fcc_a1#01_p0 new-name=NbC(deform)                                    $ Rename series 

$ ----------------------------------- ADDING FURTHER PLOTS -----------------------------------------
$ Define plot properties: Strain rate
create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.                                                                                     $ Create a new plot
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Strain rate / s<sup>-1</sup>                                                                      $ Axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=eps_dot                                                                        $ Add series
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines

$ Define plot properties: Dislocation density
create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.                                                                                     $ Create a new plot
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Dislocation density / m<sup>-2</sup>                                                              $ Axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=dd_tot$austenite                                                               $ Add series
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines

$ Define plot properties: Nucleation rate
create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.                                                                                     $ Create a new plot
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=NbC nucleation rate / m<sup>-3</sup>s<sup>-1</sup>                                                $ Axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-type=log                                                                                                $ Axis scaling type
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-scaling=1..                                                                                             $ Axis scaling range
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=nucl_rate$fcc_a1#01_p0                                                         $ Add series
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines

$ Define plot properties: Pipe diffusion enhancement
create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.                                                                                     $ Create a new plot
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Pipe diffusion correction factor                                                                  $ Axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=Pipe_dcf$austenite$*                                                           $ Add series
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                                                                        $ Y-Axis major gridlines
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                                                                        $ X-Axis major gridlines




